    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response DTO needed a new derived `contactPreference` field, computed at read time.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, producing `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the field in like the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`): a `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName = \"contactPreference\")` plus a `@Named(\"contactPreference\")` method returning `EMAIL` when the owner has a non-blank email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nNo OfficeFloor YAML or function classes needed changes \u2014 the GET pipeline already responds via `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the new derived field flows through automatically.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the rest of the suite pass.",
