    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `contactPreference` mapping follows the established pattern in this mapper exactly: a `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName = ...)` on `toOwnerDto` paired with a `@Named` default method, matching the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `locality` derived fields. \n\n- The logic sits in the right unit \u2014 deriving a read-time DTO field from the entity is precisely what these `@Named` mapper methods already do; it's not business logic that belongs elsewhere.\n- No duplication, and the mapper isn't becoming a catch-all \u2014 it's already the designated home for computed DTO fields, and this is one more of the same kind.\n- The method is small, self-contained, and reads naturally alongside its siblings.\n- The OpenAPI addition mirrors the surrounding `readOnly` derived properties (e.g. `locality`) with an appropriate enum and a clear description, which is what generates `ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural.",
